# HMAC known answers.
# hi is RFC 2104 / RFC 4231 test case 1 (20 bytes of 0x0b, "Hi There").
# long-key is RFC 4231 test case 6: the key is longer than every block here,
# so the implementation has to hash the key down first.
# empty-msg is the empty message under the three-byte key "key".
# make check-oracle recomputes these with the pinned OpenSSL.
primitive hmac

case sha1-hi
hash sha1
key 0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b0b
msg 4869205468657265
mac b617318655057264e28bc0b6fb378c8ef146be00

case sha256-hi
